# A call to an undefined function inside a CONCRETE function body must FAIL the
# compile under BOTH compilers (issues/fixed/self-hosted-compile-swallows-undefined-call.md).
# It used to be worse than a wrong diagnostic: the self-hosted compiler exited 0
# and emitted a runnable binary that did nothing, because the def-time body eval
# swallowed the error and codegen emitted the body MINUS the failing call. A
# typo became a silent no-op program.
#
# This is the third sibling of ptr-type-safe-code and await-nested-in-if-condition
# — the body-level gates that case's opts file calls "deliberately NOT cases yet".
# It is a case now because the swallow re-raises undefined-variable rejections
# from the concrete-function site (generic bodies stay lenient: their type params
# are legitimately unbound until specialization).
#
# stdout=ignore: the binaries identify fatal errors differently (TS an uncaught
# throw with a stack, yo-self a "yo-self: error:" line) — rc parity is the
# assertion, and rc parity is exactly what was broken.
# stdout_keep_match (P2.5 step 15): this case previously used stdout=ignore,
# which ANY failure satisfied. The kept substring is the probe-verified
# SHARED diagnostic - both compilers must emit it, so the case asserts THE
# failure, not just A failure.
stdout_keep_match=Variable "this_function_does_not_exist" not found
timeout=120
